{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1469124-what-would-you-like-to-see-in-a-mythic-america-supplement","id":1469124,"title":"What would you like to see in a \"Mythic America\" supplement?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-11-28T14:07:30-08:00","id":1469124,"title":"What would you like to see in a \"Mythic America\" supplement?","content":"I'm working on a custom supplement for Scion 2e that I am eventually hoping to sell on DriveThruRPG. This supplement is partially an update of the Yankee Pantheon from Scion 1e, as well as a number of other gods representing a modern America in a globalized world. I'm happy with what I have so far, but I keep on going back and forth on what I should be including. <br /> <br /> Aside from an expanded Pantheon and Pantheon-specific purviews, what would you like to see in a &quot;Mythic American&quot; supplement? Birthrights? Titans? Titanspawn? Terra Incognitae? <br /> <br /> Thanks!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27195-brokenimage321","name":"brokenimage321","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-29T15:46:31-08:00","id":1469209,"title":"","content":"America's Terra Incognitae would be good, from the Big Rock Candy Mountain to Ditty-Wah-Ditty America's down home utopian Maroon society. <br /> <br /> American mantles, including those mantles trying to redeem themselves. <br /> <br /> A few of America's mythic beasts would be grand. <br /> <br /> Some examples of older deities from the Native American Traditions that have made special adaptations to modern America. Example: By now Bugs Bunny has a mantle, he'd be about the only cartoon character that would. What Native American tricksters might want that mantle and why could be fascinating.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-30T03:56:17-08:00","id":1469243,"title":"","content":"The fearsome creatures of lumberjack tales,Iike the hide behind. <br /> <br /> And the alien gods of the najavo, which are obviously titans. <br /> <br /> And obviously the big rock candy mountain.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26173-evtrax","name":"evtrax","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"228"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-05T21:06:27-08:00","id":1469693,"title":"","content":"The Biggest Ball of Twine in Minnesota.<br /> <br /> The mythical version of Route 66.<br /> <br /> The lost State of Franklin.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-06T00:32:38-08:00","id":1469700,"title":"","content":"Maybe some American centric Cryptids like Mothman, the Jackalope, Jersey Devil, etc.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27210-fereality","name":"fereality","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27210_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-06T01:02:38-08:00","id":1469704,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>fereality</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1469124-what-would-you-like-to-see-in-a-mythic-america-supplement?p=1469700#post1469700\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe some American centric Cryptids like Mothman, the Jackalope, Jersey Devil, etc.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Red Dwarf of Detroit (yes it is a real thing)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-06T07:14:54-08:00","id":1469726,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1469124-what-would-you-like-to-see-in-a-mythic-america-supplement?p=1469704#post1469704\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Red Dwarf of Detroit (yes it is a real thing)</div> </div> </div> </div>When Detroit was a French fort the Lutin was there. A rare American fairy, and one that scares gangsters and gang kids alike.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-08T14:23:05-08:00","id":1469956,"title":"","content":"Although it's brutally hard to get a copy Hal Rammel's &quot;Nowhere in America: The Big Rock Candy Mountain and other Comic Utopias&quot; is a grand source for American Terra Incognitae.<br /> <br /> Another book to look at for Mythic America (although the author is a mega creep) is &quot;The Pirate Utopias&quot; by Peter Lamborn Wilson. Vile as the author is, this is an insightful book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":857,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","user":"Astromancer","date":". 12-08-2021, 05:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-09T18:42:42-08:00","id":1470098,"title":"","content":"Around 25+ years ago, I came across a sourcebook for some game or another - I can't even begin to guess, it may have even been some weird system-neutral thing - that had a chapter about &quot;The 13th Floor&quot;. Basically it was this warped pocket dimension which was supposed to be that missing 13th floor from all the buildings that didn't have them (per the urban legend/folklore). It was sort of goofy in execution, but the idea always stuck with me as an interesting concept.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-11T18:49:46-08:00","id":1470254,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1469124-what-would-you-like-to-see-in-a-mythic-america-supplement?p=1470098#post1470098\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Around 25+ years ago, I came across a sourcebook for some game or another - I can't even begin to guess, it may have even been some weird system-neutral thing - that had a chapter about &quot;The 13th Floor&quot;. Basically it was this warped pocket dimension which was supposed to be that missing 13th floor from all the buildings that didn't have them (per the urban legend/folklore). It was sort of goofy in execution, but the idea always stuck with me as an interesting concept.</div> </div> </div> </div>I remember something like that in a couple of books, gaming and otherwise.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27210-fereality","name":"fereality","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27210_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-12T00:48:02-08:00","id":1470263,"title":"","content":"The Mystery Spot in California. Maybe have it be a place where multiple Terra incognita touch and that's why things get wonky.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/490-omenseer","name":"omenseer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar490_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"987"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-12T01:09:55-08:00","id":1470264,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>omenseer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1469124-what-would-you-like-to-see-in-a-mythic-america-supplement?p=1470263#post1470263\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Mystery Spot in California. Maybe have it be a place where multiple Terra incognita touch and that's why things get wonky.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> It remind my a Mystery Shack from <b>Gravity Falls</b> series <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=X2DUpDxFJyg\" data-code=\"X2DUpDxFJyg\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/X2DUpDxFJyg/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-12T11:19:28-08:00","id":1470287,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1469124-what-would-you-like-to-see-in-a-mythic-america-supplement?p=1470264#post1470264\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> It remind my a Mystery Shack from <b>Gravity Falls</b> series <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=X2DUpDxFJyg\" data-code=\"X2DUpDxFJyg\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/X2DUpDxFJyg/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div></div> </div> </div> </div>Always a fun comparison.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/490-omenseer","name":"omenseer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar490_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"987"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-13T14:19:15-08:00","id":1470376,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1469124-what-would-you-like-to-see-in-a-mythic-america-supplement?p=1470264#post1470264\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It remind my a Mystery Shack from <b>Gravity Falls</b> series <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>I've actually been tooling around the idea of a fanfic with the Shack Crew (Stan, Ford, Mabel, Dipper, Wendy, &amp; Pacifica. Maybe Soos.) as a band of Scions. Though really Stan &amp; Ford are Demigods and the kids are heroes. Wendy is the Daughter of a demigod (Manly Dan, demigod Scion of Paul Bunyan) and her mother a Scion who has ascended to godhood. <br /> Mostly 1e based as I don't have any 2e books.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27210-fereality","name":"fereality","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27210_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-09T14:57:27-08:00","id":1474328,"title":"","content":"I saw over on reddit r/gravityfalls that Alex Hirsh did Gravity Falls as a homage to Erie Indiana a show from back in the 90's. Does anyone else remember that series? <br /> <br /> How about Columbia/Lady Liberty as Nokomis from Longfellow's Song of Hiawatha. <br /> <br /> There's the Bunny Man from both Weird Virginia and Chasing American Monsters.<br /> <br /> I think of Pecos Bill as a scion of Coyote.<br /> <br /> American Indian Myths and Legends mentions the Adventures of Great Rabbit. Known as Mahtigwess among the Passamaquoddy and Micmac. Bugs Bunny could be his mantel in the modern world.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1869-moonwolf8","name":"moonwolf8","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-30T09:07:37-07:00","id":1482375,"title":"","content":"&quot;Pow-wows or the Long-Lost Friend&quot; by John George Hohman first published in 1820 and referenced by Manly Wade Wellman in his Silver John stories. &quot;Aradia: Gospel of the Witches&quot; by Charles G. Leland first published in 1899.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1869-moonwolf8","name":"moonwolf8","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"112"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}